WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 9:
Thinking, Feelings, and Imagination.

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.380
Welcome to the last unit of Year 3!

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.560
This unit is all about the world inside your head —
your thinking, your feelings, and your imagination.

4
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:22.120
You will learn words for ideas and emotions,
like idea, sense, reason, sadness, and experience.

5
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.660
You will learn how to imagine new things, how to make a
choice, and how to suggest ideas kindly to your friends.

6
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:37.100
You will read about children in a coastal East African town
who fill a special Box of Ideas with their dreams and hopes.

7
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.180
By the end, you will be able to
talk about what you think and feel,

8
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.540
and use your imagination to write your own ideas down.

9
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.780
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:58.120
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
use abstract nouns like idea, reason, experience,

11
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.400
and sadness to talk about thoughts and feelings.

12
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.860
you will also say what you imagine
and describe pictures in your mind.

13
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.240
you will also give a reason for something using because.

14
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.260
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:20.460
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
idea, imagine, reason, purpose, choice, sense.

16
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:26.340
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.200
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:36.740
The reading sequence includes The Box of Ideas
at School and Feelings Are Not Bad or Good.

19
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:38.840
Read actively.

20
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:44.360
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:48.500
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.420
The first language focus is Abstract Nouns.

23
00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:00.700
An abstract noun is a word for something you cannot see,
touch, or hold — like a feeling, a quality, or an idea.

24
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.760
Words like idea, experience, sadness,
and kindness are abstract nouns.

25
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.140
They let you talk about what is inside your mind and heart.

26
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:18.200
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.500
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Share an Idea.

28
00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.920
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.900
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.440
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.000
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:42.440
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.400
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.280
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
